# Everything in this repo is deployed to a Linux VM, and several files are
# shipped verbatim by pyinfra's files.put (shell scripts, systemd units, a
# Dockerfile). A CRLF shebang makes the kernel look for an interpreter named
# "/bin/sh\r", which surfaces as the baffling "sh: 1: <script>: not found" even
# though the file is plainly there.
#
# Without this, a checkout on a machine with core.autocrlf=true ships broken
# scripts. Pin the working tree to LF regardless of the local git config.
* text=auto eol=lf
